From: RG DS <rgds@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] gles: upload the vertex and index buffers whole

GlBuffer::update wrote each frame with glBufferSubData over the start of a
buffer the GPU could still be reading (last frame's vertices). Panfrost then
flushes and waits for the GPU before every upload ("Synchronized write"): on
the RG DS (Mali-G52) the drawing thread spent about a third of each frame in
that wait, and Crazy Taxi drove at ~30 fps. glBufferData lets the driver drop
the old contents and take a fresh buffer: the same drive now runs at 55-60 fps.

--- a/core/rend/gles/gles.h
+++ b/core/rend/gles/gles.h
@@ -143,15 +143,12 @@
 	void update(const void *data, GLsizeiptr size)
 	{
 		bind();
-		if (size > this->size)
-		{
-			glBufferData(type, size, data, usage);
-			this->size = size;
-		}
-		else
-		{
-			glBufferSubData(type, 0, size, data);
-		}
+		// RG DS: the whole buffer anew each frame. glBufferSubData over part of a buffer the GPU may still be reading
+		// (last frame's vertices) made Panfrost flush and wait for the GPU on every upload ("Synchronized write"):
+		// the drawing thread spent a third of each frame in that wait on the RG DS. glBufferData lets the driver
+		// discard the old contents and take a fresh buffer instead.
+		glBufferData(type, size, data, usage);
+		this->size = size;
 	}
 
 private:
